author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Shared prerequisites occur once per plan; every target has fresh supporting evidence, a selected supporting check, or an explicit gap; bounded fixtures prove exact minimum cost below rerunning every approved check."
release: 2026.10.29
resolution: "Delivered by PR #226 (491456c): Choose the cheapest approved checks to re-verify expired claims"
expected_result: "Shared prerequisites occur once per plan; every target has fresh supporting evidence, a selected supporting check, or an explicit gap; bounded fixtures prove exact minimum cost below rerunning every approved check."
actual_result: "PR #226 merged at 2026-10-29T04:53:41Z as 491456c; required CI passed on the merged head."
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T03:47:56.066Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core SDK assurance supplies canonical receipts, expiry validity, complete tracker reads and status roles; no least-cost rerun compiler found. pm-ops evidence-expiry classifies retained health/coverage/recovery evidence, diagnostic-plans owns approved catalog execution and budgets. pm-brief acquires missing evidence, pm-evidence owns source citations, pm-rlm owns decomposition; none compiles expired claims into a minimum-cost dependency closure. Scope: read-only planning, exact integer costs, bounded exhaustive solver, explicit approval/dependency gaps, no tracker writes or journal. No transaction-isolation claim; commitWorkspaceTransaction does not isolate ordinary writers (pm-cli#1620). Freshness is observed, planned checks are conditional until rerun and new receipts are accepted."
  "2026-10-29T03:53:27.732Z",codex-agent,"Implementation boundary: strict version 1 input (32 claims, 16 targets, 18 checks), exhaustive dependency-closed subset search with exact safe-integer costs and deterministic ties. SDK expiry is reused for CLI freshness; pure SDK compilation trusts caller-declared evidence provenance. Shared prerequisites appear once in topological order. Native tracker import/export/sync, recovery journals, idempotency keys, status-name interpretation and mutation leases are absent by design. A 500-sequence BigInt/set reference model caught an unapproved-leaf cache omission during development; regression covers approval, dependency cycles, gaps, replay, CRLF and finite outputs. Native fields and relationships are compared via SDK readback, without custom normalization."
  "2026-10-29T03:59:33.006Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public main snapshot validation: 162 items, 332 files, SDK probes checked 11 schema types, 162 items and 2296 history entries. Two declared repair targets selected three checks with the shared prerequisite once; declared integer cost 6 versus all-approved baseline 26 (saved 20). Repeated plans identical; every tracker byte unchanged; no Git required. Packet: JSON 868 bytes, TOON 830 bytes. Missing accepted receipts remain two conditional rerun claims, not assertions of fresh health/recovery. Targeted regression also dispatches existing diagnostic catalog probes exactly once and preserves native fields/relationships through SDK readback."
  "2026-10-29T04:07:50.293Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in an owned disposable copy, replace only the compiler selection with rerun-all executable approved checks. The exact closure regression fails at 16 versus expected 6 (assertion failure, not import failure). Fixed worktree is untouched and the linked regression is rerun. Local typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings (42 modules/331 declarations) and zero-duplication gate passed. Stored targeted c8 report covers the new planner at 100% statements, branches and functions. A test-run configuration refusal was retained; the rerun uses pm-context none with workspace-context snapshot as required by the pinned test runner."
  "2026-10-29T04:08:41.321Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm regression passed: 8 tests, 8 passed, 0 failed/skipped/canceled, including 500 sequences / 3000 model operations and every observed history-read interleaving. Exact command: pm test ops-reverification --run --progress --pm-context none --workspace-context snapshot --override-linked-pm-context --override-linked-workspace-context. Full npm/Bun release gates and six packed launch modes run in existing CI; the PR will carry final-head run URLs and counts, without later tracker-only pushes invalidating that evidence. Remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-29T04:13:15.463Z",codex-agent,"Final test-completeness check adds explicit omitted-now coverage in both the injected command harness and the actual installed CLI. This verifies the optional clock default, complements malformed supplied-clock refusal, and preserves the full branch threshold in CI. Dedicated installed-command regression passed with the same plan as the explicit expired instant. Final CI evidence will use the subsequent pushed head."
  "2026-10-29T04:31:20.414Z",codex-agent,"CI evidence and correction: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40816554332 (head eab0a4f) completed the Node 22 test suite: 1505 tests, 1501 passed, 2 failed, 2 optional configured-repository real-data tests skipped; aggregate source coverage 100/100/100/100. Both failures were the independent renderer-ownership test literal omitting the new ops reverify command. Updated that literal without weakening its assertions; focused renderer regression now passes 7/7 with zero skips. Feature tests passed in the full suite. Node 22/26 Windows consumers and CodeQL passed on that head. New-head npm and Bun release gates and six-mode packed acceptance remain pending; current run links and final counts are kept in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/226. No SDK defect was established. Existing normal-environment pinned/global extension skew is avoided by isolated strict-health validation."
